A Route's destroy leaves its channel taken.
The channel table would name a freed object, and the channel could never be bound again;
the channel table names exactly the bound Routes.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: channel table names a route that is gone
Witness: fuzz route-dies-with-pool

diff --git a/kernel/route.c b/kernel/route.c
--- a/kernel/route.c
+++ b/kernel/route.c
@@ -63,7 +63,6 @@ void route_forget(struct route *r)
     if (r->armed) {
         route_arm(r, false);
     }
-    channel_route[r->channel - ROUTE_FIRST] = 0;
 }
 
 #if ROUTER_FAKE
